{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WqRKGhMmZo2M9uA5Wn3Cun","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline by regenerating GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Components: cmd/ (utility implementations), pkg/sys (syscalls), pkg/format (formatting), pkg/testutils (differential testing), pkg/encutil (encoding utilities), pkg/hashutil (hash computation), pkg/sizeparse (size parsing), magefiles/ (build automation).\n\n**Current state**: Releases 00.0 through 09.0 have all requirements completed (no \"ready\" R-items remain in requirement_states). The earliest release with ready requirements is **release 09.1** — the encoding utilities batch (base32, base64, basenc). The shared pkg/encutil library is already implemented.\n\n**Current release**: 09.1 — three encoding utilities need implementation:\n- cmd/base32 (srd079-base32: 11 requirements R1.1-R3.3, all ready)\n- cmd/base64 (srd080-base64: 11 requirements R1.1-R3.3, all ready)\n- cmd/basenc (srd081-basenc: 12 requirements R1.1-R3.4, all ready)\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 09.1 is the earliest incomplete release. All three utilities share the implemented pkg/encutil library. No blocking dependencies. Alphabetical ordering: base32 → base64 → basenc.\n\nWith the 4-task limit, I'll complete cmd/base32 (3 implementation tasks + 1 test task). base64 and basenc follow in future sessions.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\n```\nTask 0: srd079-base32 R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd079-base32 R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1), R2.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd079-base32 R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTa